# Spec 027 — UI review

Status: Draft
Owner: <you>
Related: GitHub #20; 025 (shared shell and tokens), 010 (target sizes),
022-024 (DriveCheap screens)

## Overview

Make both products look like one finished site. Fix the layout, typography and
copy problems that read as unfinished, starting with the owner's screenshot of
`/drive-cheap/checklist`. Nothing in this spec changes a calculation.

## Context

A headless pass on 2026-11-11 covered every surface at 1280 and 390 px wide:
landing, the LiveNear map, the detail panel (WA and Oslo), About, and the
DriveCheap screens Situation, Market, Checklist, Compare, Curves and Option
detail. It found the problems below, which the requirements address:

- **Checklist cards:** they have no gap between them (`.cars-checklist` has no
  CSS rule), and their headings sit on the card border because a flush card
  uses an unpadded `__head`.
- **Developer text on screen:**
  - "Pending rule ev_vat_2027_proposed".
  - Option detail values and notes showing `first_after_months`, `repair_ev_factor`, `rates.yaml (inspection_fee_nok)`.
  - "Default estimate (engine/defaults.py)".
  - "cohort tesla-model3-lr-awd:2019 at 112709 km".
  - About a dozen inputs whose source reads "Placeholder".
- **Fonts:** 13 control types on the map panel (Go, the region select, the
  product switcher, Add second workplace, the matches rows, About, the zoom
  buttons) render in the browser default font, because no rule sets
  `font: inherit`. Some DriveCheap controls do the same.
- **Dates:** shown as raw ISO ("Due 2027-01-01", "Prices as of 2026-11-02").
- **Units:** DriveCheap inputs say "NOK" next to results that say "kr".
- **Phone layout:**
  - Checklist checkboxes sit on their own line above the title.
  - The step navigation leaves "5 Checklist" alone on a second line.
  - A 720px media rule adds padding back to flush cards.
- **Colours:** DriveCheap keeps its own border, green, neutral and shadow values
  beside the shared tokens from 025, and `styles.css` still has about 26 kinds
  of literal colour outside `:root`. Font sizes are scattered px values in both
  stylesheets.

## Requirements

### Layout

- **R1 — Checklist sections.** Checklist sections are separated like other
  DriveCheap cards, and each section heading has the same inner padding as
  other card headings.
- **R2 — Checklist rows on phones.** At 390px the checkbox stays beside the
  item title, and the tag and due badges sit under the text.
- **R3 — Flush cards on phones.** Cards designed without padding (lists and
  tables) stay that way at every width.
- **R4 — Step navigation on phones.** At 390px the five DriveCheap steps sit on
  one row, scrolling sideways if needed, and never leave a single step alone on
  a second line.

### Copy

- **R5 — No internal identifiers.** No rule id, config key, file name, model
  version or cohort id appears in visible text or in the checklist download.
  - Pending rules are described in words, for example "Proposed change, not yet law: …".
  - The inspection cycle reads like "First at 48 months, then every 24 months".
  - Model provenance reads like "Market model, 93 comparable sales". The
    version moves to a tooltip.
- **R6 — Plain source labels.** An input with no external source is labelled
  "Typical value" or "Your input" instead of "Placeholder". It stays marked as an
  estimate with its written basis, as CLAUDE.md requires; only the label changes.
- **R7 — Dates.** Dates in both products read as "1 Jan 2027", not ISO. This
  covers due badges, "Prices as of", source dates and the next deadline.
  Machine formats such as URLs, the API and the checklist file's metadata are
  unchanged.
- **R8 — Units.** DriveCheap uses "kr" for money everywhere, including input
  suffixes. "NOK" appears only where a currency code is expected.

### Visual system

- **R9 — Fonts.** Every button, input, select and textarea uses the site font.
- **R10 — Colour tokens.**
  - DriveCheap's border, positive green, neutrals and shadow use the shared
    025 tokens.
  - Repeated literal colours in `styles.css` and the price chart move into
    named tokens.
  - Estimate, error, chart-series and map-ramp colours keep their own named
    tokens or data.
- **R11 — Type scale.** Both stylesheets take font sizes from one shared set
  of `--fs-*` tokens. DriveCheap's 15px reading size and the map panel's 13px
  stay different on purpose.

## Non-functional / Constraints

- No change to any number, ranking or calculation. Golden scenarios and engine
  tests pass unchanged.
- Spec 010 target sizes and contrast still hold. Text colours stay at or above
  4.5:1.
- No new dependencies.

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] At both widths the checklist matches R1-R3: separated cards, padded
      headings, checkbox beside the title.
- [ ] At 390px the step navigation never leaves a single step on its own row (R4).
- [ ] A rendered-page scan of every surface finds no snake_case identifier or
      file name, and the checklist download has none (R5).
- [ ] No visible "Placeholder" source label; estimates still show their basis (R6).
- [ ] No ISO date in visible text on either product (R7).
- [ ] DriveCheap money inputs show "kr" (R8).
- [ ] A computed-style scan finds no form control whose font differs from the
      body's (R9).
- [ ] `cars.css` defines no border, positive, neutral or shadow colour of its
      own, and `styles.css` has no repeated literal colour outside `:root` (R10).
- [ ] Font sizes come from `--fs-*` tokens (R11).
- [ ] Before and after screenshots of every surface at 1280 and 390px.
- [ ] `npm run test`, `npm run build`, `pytest`, `ruff check .` pass, with
      golden scenarios unchanged.

## Out of Scope (explicit)

- Translation and number formats per language (spec 028, #19).
- Redesigning any screen, or changing which information a screen shows.
- The browser's own date-picker format (mm/dd/yyyy), which follows the
  browser's locale. Spec 028 sets the page language.
- Backend explanatory prose beyond removing identifiers (R5).

## Open Questions (resolve in review)

None open. The owner approved the spec, including the R6 wording ("Typical
value", "Your input").

## Verification notes

R1-R4, R9-R11 → the screenshot tour plus a computed-style scan; R5, R7 → a
rendered-text scan for snake_case, file names and ISO dates, plus unit tests on
the checklist copy and the date formatter; R6, R8 → unit tests and
screenshots. The human verifies; the implementing agent does not self-certify
done.

Results, 2026-11-12. A headless tour of 10 surfaces at 1280 and 390px, on a
production build with sample data, found:

- no form control in a font other than the body's, including MapLibre's own
  buttons;
- no snake_case id, file name, ISO date, "Placeholder" or "NOK" in visible text;
- no sideways page overflow;
- the DriveCheap steps on one row;
- no page errors.

Implementation notes:

- "Placeholder" and "Owner input" remain in the data files and are relabelled
  at display time (`plainSource`), so no bundle was rebuilt.
- Code-generated sources and the two prose notes that named config keys were
  rewritten in the backend.
- `tests/cars/test_properties.py` could not run locally: Windows Application
  Control blocks a hypothesis DLL. The other 258 backend tests pass.
